{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes safe, efficient exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, one-shot turn recoveries. Full_rotate is reserved for deliberate search in clear states only. All obstacle recoveries are deterministic and do not allow forward or random_walk actions until the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect the robot's hardware and sensor interface.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, deterministic turn recovery on obstacles, and quick return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
